It is Tuesday morning.
I have a bicycle.
But the bicycle is broken.
I push my bicycle to a repair shop.
The repair shop is near my flat.
I go into the repair shop.
A mechanic is there.
"Good morning," I say.
"My bicycle is broken."
"Good morning," says the mechanic.
He looks at the bicycle.
"That is no problem," he says.
"When will the bicycle be ready?" I ask.
"Come on Wednesday afternoon," says the mechanic.
"At what time?" I ask.
"At half past three," he says.
"Yes, half past three is good," I say.
I leave my bicycle in the repair shop.
Then I go to the U-Bahn.
I take the U-Bahn to the office every day.
